title: An equality test folded into a row that xfail(run=False) never runs
note: Found by D-192's review; it passed on main c06b10d3. A strict xfail is
note2: not read as a disabled row, but run=False keeps pytest from running the
note3: row at all, so checked(50) is no longer checked. A live row's own marks
note4: are not in its proof key, so the unit now proves nothing.
=== env ===
app
=== head: app.py ===
def checked(x):
    if not 0 <= x <= 100:
        raise ValueError(x)
    return x
=== before: test_app.py ===
import pytest
from app import checked


def test_ok():
    assert checked(50) == 50
=== after: test_app.py ===
import pytest
from app import checked


@pytest.mark.parametrize("ok", [pytest.param(50, marks=pytest.mark.xfail(run=False, strict=True))])
def test_valid(ok):
    assert checked(ok) == ok
